---
name: release
description: Cut a release. Bumps the version, runs the full gate, commits, tags{% if license != "Proprietary" %}, and pushes the tag so the release workflow publishes to PyPI{% endif %}. User-invoked only.
argument-hint: major | minor | patch
disable-model-invocation: true
---

Release bump: $ARGUMENTS

1. Preconditions: `git status` is clean, the current branch is the default
   branch, and `$ARGUMENTS` is one of `major`, `minor`, `patch`. Stop
   otherwise.
2. Gate first: `uv run nox`. Nothing is released from a failing tree.
3. Bump: `uv run nox -s bump -- $ARGUMENTS`.{% if use_rust %} This also updates
   the Cargo workspace version and `Cargo.lock`.{% endif %} Show the diff and
   the new version from `uv version --short`.
4. Commit and tag:

       git commit -am "Release v$(uv version --short)"
       git tag "v$(uv version --short)"
{% if license != "Proprietary" %}
5. Confirm with the user, then `git push --follow-tags`. The tag runs
   `.github/workflows/release.yml`, which checks that the tag matches the
   project version and publishes with trusted publishing.
{%- else %}
5. Stop here. This project is proprietary: there is no release workflow and
   no publish step. Pushing is the user's call.
{%- endif %}
